---
// backup: one kernel written by hand, three times ('intro to kernel writing on blackhole', sep 2026)
import { Bars } from 'slides/viz';
import Math from 'slides/Math';
import f from '../facts.json';
const r = f.rmsnorm;
---
<header>
  <div class="section">backup · writing a kernel by hand</div>
  <h2>where the work runs inside a core decides the speed</h2>
  <p class="sub">rmsnorm: rescales a vector of 2048 numbers. it runs twice in every layer of llama</p>
</header>
<div class="rms">
  <div class="left">
    <Math block tex={String.raw`\mathrm{rmsnorm}(x) = \gamma \odot \dfrac{x}{\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{d}\sum_i x_i^2 + \epsilon}}`} />
    <ul>
      <li>the sum and square root need the <b>vector engine</b>: precise, but slower</li>
      <li>multiplying by the weights <span class="g">γ</span> doesn’t depend on the sum, so it can move to the <b>matrix engine</b> and run alongside</li>
      <li>tuning how instructions are issued wins the rest</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="right">
    <h3>cycles for one rmsnorm (lower is better)</h3>
    <div class="bigbars"><Bars values={[r.vector_only, r.hybrid, r.tuned]} labels={['all on the vector engine', 'split across both engines', 'tuned']}
      max={1600} width={240} fmtV={(v) => v.toLocaleString('en-US')} hl={2} color="var(--good)" /></div>
    <p class="cap">{Number(((1 - r.tuned / r.vector_only) * 100).toFixed(0))}% fewer cycles than the first version, same math</p>
  </div>
</div>
<style>
  .rms { display: flex; gap: 70px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .left { width: 700px; font-size: 26px; }
  .left ul { margin-top: 14px; }
  .left li { margin: 8px 0; }
  .g { font-family: var(--mono); }
  .right { width: 680px; font-size: 24px; }
  .right h3 { font-size: 24px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }
  .bigbars { font-size: 38px; }
  .bigbars :global(.bars) { row-gap: 16px; }
  .cap { font-size: 22px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 12px; }
</style>
